2. CONVENTIONS, UNITS AND RESPONSE UNITS

R denotes all real numbers. sqrt is the principal nonnegative real square root.
Interval brackets denote included endpoints; parentheses denote exclusions.
Infinity is a limit, never an included endpoint or a plotted finite point.
Each requested graph is the entire real-domain function, not a finite viewport.
Algebraic simplification is always subject to the ORIGINAL formula's domain.
An omitted point with a finite limit is a hole. An infinite limit at an excluded
abscissa is a vertical asymptote, not a finite hole marker.
Coordinates and x/y values have no physical units specified; they are abstract
real numbers. No length, angle, time or unit conversion is authorized or needed.

Natural independent mathematical units:
  U1 = 1103a: complete graph of 1/|x|
  U2 = 1103b: complete graph of 1/sqrt(x)
  U3 = 1103c: complete graph of x^3/|x|
  U4 = 1104a: complete graph of sqrt(x^2)+x
  U5 = 1104b: complete graph of sqrt(x^2)-x
  U6 = 1104c: complete graph of |x+2|
  U7 = 1104d: complete graph of |x-1|
  U8 = 1105: complete graph of x+1/x
Each is a whole-graph task. Domain, sign cases, branch geometry, actual included
points, holes, shifts, extrema and limiting behavior cannot silently be replaced
by an isolated numeric cell. Grouping/splitting candidate questions is not decided
here because no view has been authorized. If drawing later becomes recognition,
the loss of independent construction must be recorded in the later fidelity gate.
